{"id": "EUVD-2026-103463", "enisaUuid": "7d9b1643-6bb4-358c-8533-1dd021b36405", "description": "smpeg through 2.0.0 contains an integer underflow vulnerability in stream_header() in MPEGsystem.cpp that allows attackers to wrap packet_size by declaring an undersized packet length. Attackers can supply a crafted MPEG file opened via SMPEG_new, SMPEG_new_rwops or SMPEG_new_data to trigger a reachable assertion or out-of-bounds copy, crashing the application.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T11:38:32", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-18T12:23:31", "baseScore": 6.8, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:L/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:P/VC:N/VI:N/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@haindpwn/smpeg-system-header-stream-table-oob-read", "https://github.com/icculus/smpeg/blob/d188dc111f4817288718705e4a84e248803ccfdc/MPEGsystem.cpp#L295-L350", "https://github.com/icculus/smpeg/blob/d188dc111f4817288718705e4a84e248803ccfdc/MPEGsystem.cpp#L777", "https://github.com/icculus/smpeg", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/smpeg-through-2.0.0-integer-underflow-via-stream-header-in-mpegsystem-cpp"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-112010", "GHSA-xc26-7mh2-w5rr"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.13, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "454a222a-0957-3743-8c1b-0dae875ec8f7", "product": {"name": "smpeg", "vendor": {"name": "icculus"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22642.0.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "6caffe5b-f688-3e94-8b64-153a261c0c8a", "vendor": {"name": "icculus"}}], "isExploited": false}